<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuelan authorities continue to detain President Maduro, who is reported to be studying religion and reading the Bible and Quran while incarcerated, as his wife seeks her release. The U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth faces multiple impeachment resolutions from Rep. Thomas Massie and other Republicans, citing the Iran war, boat strikes and a raid linked to Maduro. Trump publicly defends Hegseth against the impeachment push. The conflict environment remains active, with the UCDP reporting 2 battle-related deaths in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE0ya1dZNzJwTmJzelRlVUxSQzJQU2Q5NExhbC1NbjFoN2J3Yzk2RU5PaEZoSm9mdEdjY2VkUUVOazBQUVF0Z3J5Z1B6LXdiMVdtbDdaOGY4bGpVdzVqLTNuVVBNMENkaHhtbm5iWC1JRUtwUG9DaVQ4?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3373848/hegseth-calls-iran-war-necessary-and-waves-noise-expected-impeachment-push&quot;&gt;South China Morning Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE5hZGNWSjdJRzV6bURoY25jdDktbGFzZXV3aV9kRU0xV2pRVkw5bGtyVE9qM3RoaUV1SlhtOEd1elpxZTVxYmlkeGZaR3dGTXVVNWVTc1lwOE1DVFE1X1ZFanlkR2pXZ0N2S1FwT3FPSlBaQTVzUE1j?oc=5&quot;&gt;Cronkite News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxQTE93M3M0b1lFcWw3S0hqWmhZZl8xUktTdzltQklqeUF0VnlfemVjSlNBcC1ZdEQxRm1FbVRpN2dzcUw1SkE0S1lRT2haajJfcTBFcTRKR1hQZEZvYWNQRmJObm5hNlRvY1YxekZSYVhLREkwTFZMTUxadlNsRFFYTWVfc3plQTZqaFhj?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Boston Globe&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxONzVGSi13ZklBN3Q2R1VWb1o3VzhTekRTV0t1VzVfVjJIcHRoQVhOMnhJaFNuQzY3M1pUY0cwUEYzMDRLWUdZcGUxbk5jWHJ4TzVaWlhGbHpJc2tHM3YwdHJUTnZhU01ITnBoNXZmcFZKeGtzWkJDNGE3VkE5MjR0MV9oQTl0ODIyLTFxTlg0Z3pfWDl6MW9qVzlQZVRnV